Description: Interactive Shiny dashboard for exploring the American Authorship
    Database (1860-1920), a comprehensive collection of publishing and sales
    data from major American publishers during the late 19th and early 20th
    centuries. The database includes 630+ book entries with sales data spanning
    63 years, sourced from major publisher archives including Houghton Mifflin,
    Harper & Brothers, Scribner, and J. B. Lippincott.
